// S176 CI-owned collision scenario: three agents share ONE wash basin and ONE
// latrine at a self-sufficient camp over 1440 ticks under ordinary need
// pressure. Sanitation degrades under multi-agent use — the shared basin grows
// filthy (cleaned via clean_wash_basin), the shared latrine fills (emptied via
// empty_latrine or diverted to wilderness relief), and place dirtiness rises and
// decays. Proves facility-state arithmetic crossing-and-recovering via labor,
// the FND-14B belief barrier (no omniscient remote-facility reads), typed
// DegradedSelfCareOpportunity causal records, and replay equivalence.
//
// The camp is self-sufficient (water + apples + sleep + latrine + basin all
// co-located) so the run isolates sanitation contention rather than travel.
(
    seed: 176440,
    compaction_interval: 240,
    places: [
        (
            name: "Shared Camp",
            tags: [Camp, Latrine],
            place_dirtiness: (value: 0, decay_per_tick: 2, dirtiness_per_use: 60),
            latrine_fullness: (fill: 0, fill_per_use: 90, critical_threshold: 800),
            sleep_quality: (shelter: Roofed, ground_comfort: Soft, recovery_modifier: 1000),
        ),
